course: dictionary
lesson: 2015
title: Conduction: heat moving through materials
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Conduction is the way heat or electricity moves through a material from one part to another, while the material itself stays where it is. Nothing is carried along. The energy is passed from one part to the next.
explain: «Conduction passes heat through touching materials, like a pan handle getting hot.» The flame heats the metal of the pan, and the heat moves through the metal to the handle. The handle gets hot even though nobody touched the flame.
explain: Some materials are good at conduction and some are not. Metals are good conductors: a metal spoon in hot soup gets hot by conduction. Wood and plastic are poor conductors, also called insulators, so they are used for pan handles. «Conduction is heat passing through a material or between things that touch.» Check the meaning by putting it into the sentence: heat passing through a material makes sense.
fact: Conduction is one of three ways heat travels. The other two are convection and radiation.
fact: Metals are good conductors of heat and electricity.
fact: Wood and plastic are poor conductors, which means they are insulators.
fact: «Heat conduction» and «electrical conduction» are phrases you will meet in science.
fact: In conduction, energy moves through a material, but the material itself does not move.
exercise: «A metal spoon in hot soup gets hot.» What process moves the heat up the spoon? | *Conduction | Magnetism | Sound | Bouncing
exercise: Which material is a poor conductor, so it is used for pan handles? | *Wood | Copper | Iron | Steel
exercise: «Conduction passes heat through touching materials, like a pan handle getting hot.» What must happen for conduction to pass heat? | *The materials must touch | The materials must be floating in water | The materials must be in the sun | The materials must be very large
test: In conduction, does the material itself move? | Yes, it rolls away from the heat | *No, only the heat or electricity moves through it | Yes, it slides along the table | Yes, it floats up into the air
test: Which is a good conductor of heat? | Wood | Rubber | Plastic | *Copper
exam: Why is a plastic spoon a poor choice for stirring hot soup? | *Plastic is a poor conductor, so heat does not travel up it quickly | Plastic stops heat by pushing it away | Plastic conducts heat better than metal | Plastic is a metal and gets very hot
